.TH SLEEP 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
sleep \- suspend execution for seconds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B unsigned int sleep(unsigned int seconds);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sleeps for a relative interval using Linux nanosleep.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on completion, or the remaining seconds rounded up after a signal.
On another syscall error, returns the requested seconds and sets errno.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nanosleep (3crunch),
.BR sleep (3)
